    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` following the existing derived-attribute pattern in this Spring Boot PetClinic app.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` getter returning `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`. This sits alongside the existing derived getters (`getLocality()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, `getDisplayName()`), so it's exactly where this kind of logic belongs. I also extracted the email-presence check into a private `hasEmail()` helper and reused it in `getMembershipLevel()`, which previously had the check inline \u2014 so the \"email present\" rule now lives in one place.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Declared the read-only `contactPreference` string field on the `Owner` schema. The build generates `OwnerDto` from this spec, and MapStruct auto-maps the matching `getContactPreference()` getter \u2014 no mapper edits needed.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
